cy (e.g., aspirin 81mg daily).\n","    - ALLERGIES: Known allergies or adverse reactions (e.g., penicillin allergy).\n","    - REVIEW OF SYSTEMS: Systematic review of symptoms across body systems (e.g., constitutional, cardiovascular, respiratory).\n","    - VITALS: Measured vital signs (e.g., BP 120/80, HR 72).\n","    - PHYSICAL EXAM: Findings from examination (e.g., HEENT normal, abdomen soft).\n","    - RESULTS: Lab, imaging, or test results (e.g., CBC normal).\n","    - ASSESSMENT: Doctor's diagnosis or impressions (e.g., likely migraine).\n","    - ASSESSMENT AND PLAN: Combined summary of assessment and next steps (use if both are discussed together).\n","    - PLAN: Treatment recommendations, follow-up (e.g., prescribe medication, refer to specialist).\n","    - INSTRUCTIONS: Patient education or discharge instructions (e.g., take medication as directed).\n","\n","    The notes must follow this exact structure, with sections in uppercase headings. Only populate sections with relevant information from the conversation. If a section has no information (even inferred), leave it blank under the heading (do not say \"Not mentioned\" or add placeholders). Update only the sections affected by new information from the latest conversation snippet, while preserving and carrying over unchanged content from previous notes.\n","\n","    Conversation transcript so far:\n","    {conversation}\n","\n","    Previous notes:\n","    {previous_notes}\n","    \"\"\""],"metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-02-09T21:30:02.63165Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-02-09T21:30:02.632437Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-02-09T21:30:02.639794Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-02-09T21:30:02.632399Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-02-09T21:30:02.638069Z"},"id":"Fmjokr7YYteR"},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":["dataset = load_dataset(\"mkieffer/ACI-Bench\", \"aci\")"],"metadata":{"id":"RNzSA07Jl22y"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["number_of_qa_per_prompt = 4"],"metadata":{"id":"ykfcowLUlk5y"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["cvs = dataset[\"train\"][\"dialogue\"][0].split(\"\\n\")\n","qa_pairs = [\"\".join(x) for x in zip(cvs[0::2], cvs[1::2])]\n","# For when the cvs ends with a doctor speech\n","if len(cvs) % 2 == 1:\n","  qa_pairs[-1] += cvs[-1]\n","samples = []\n","for i in range(0, len(qa_pairs), number_of_qa_per_prompt):\n","    samples.append(\"\".join(qa_pairs[i:i+number_of_qa_per_prompt+1]))\n"],"metadata":{"id":"eMIb6ZRWlsCi"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["previous_notes = \"\"\n","current_conversation = \"\"\n","\n","for i, sample in enumerate(samples):\n","\n","    current_conversation += sample\n","\n","    prompt = make_prompt(current_conversation, previous_notes)\n","\n","    model_answer = get_model_answer(pipe, prompt)\n","\n","    final_answer = (\n","        model_answer\n","        .split(\"<unused95>\")[-1]\n","        # .split(\"CURRENT NOTES:\")[-1]\n","    )\n","\n","    # Application output\n","    # print(\"=\"*60)\n","    # print(\"Conversation:\")\n","    # print(\"=\"*60)\n","    # print(current_conversation)\n","    # print(\"=\"*60)\n","    # print(\"Notes:\")\n","    # print(\"=\"*60)\n","    # print(final_answer)\n","    # print(\"=\"*60)\n","\n","    # Technical output\n","    print(\"=\"*60)\n","    print(\"Model Input:\")\n","    print(\"=\"*60)\n","    print(prompt)\n","    print(\"=\"*60)\n","    print(\"Model output:\")\n","    print(\"=\"*60)\n","    print(model_answer)\n","    print(\"=\"*60)\n","\n","    previous_notes = final_answer\n"],"metadata":{"trusted":true,"id":"EmIqYW_vYteR"},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Teste usando o llama cpp\n","\n","Aqui estou usando um prompt que foi gerado com a IA do HugginFace que consegue adicionar a base dados como contexto. Pedi para ela escrever o prompt com base nas características da base de dados."],"metadata":{"id":"dklgmvDeD5eK"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["model_name = \"hungqbui/medgemma-4b-it-Q4_K_M-GGUF\"\n","model_file = \"medgemma-4b-it-q4_k_m.gguf\" # The exact filename from the repo\n","\n","# This downloads the file to your Colab local storage\n","model_path = hf_hub_download(repo_id=model_name, filename=model_file)\n","print(f\"Model downloaded to: {model_path}\")"],"metadata":{"id":"2mcI9EV73mkz"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"\n","\n","You are a real‑time medical scribe for a virtual visit.\n","For every request you will receive:\n","\n","  1. **NOTE** – the complete SOAP note that the model produced on the previous turn\n","     (it may be empty for the very first turn).\n","\n","  2. **DIALOGUE_CHUNK** – the newest lines of the doctor‑patient conversation that\n","     have not yet been incorporated into the note.\n","\n","Your job is to return a **single, complete, updated note** that reflects all\n","information that is now available.\n","\n","--------------------------------------------------------------------\n","### General Rules\n","* Keep every part of the previous note unchanged unless the new dialogue\n","  provides additional or corrected information.\n","* Add information **only** when it is **explicitly stated** or **unambiguously\n","  implied** in the dialogue.  **Never fabricate** a value that is not mentioned.\n","* When a field is mentioned but some details are missing, record what is known\n","  and note the missing part (e.g. “dose not specified”).\n","* Do not place a tentative patient impression into the **ASSESSMENT**; keep it\n","  in the HPI unless the physician makes a definitive diagnostic statement.\n","* Return **only** the updated note – no explanations, no extra text.\n","\n","--------------------------------------------------------------------\n","### What may be inferred (only when clearly present)\n","\n","| Item                     | How it can be obtained from the dialogue                |\n","|--------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|\n","| **Age & Sex**            | Direct statement (“I’m a 57‑year‑old male”) or explicit gender identifier (“I’m a dad”, “I’m a woman”). |\n","| **Chronic conditions**  | Patient or doctor says the condition (“I have diabetes”, “you’re being treated for hypertension”). |\n","| **Current medications**  | Any drug name, dose, and/or frequency that appears. If only the name is given, list it with “dose not specified”. |\n","| **Vital signs**          | Physician reads them aloud (BP, HR, RR, Temp, SpO₂). |\n","| **Physical‑exam findings**| Doctor’s description of inspection, palpation, ROM, special tests, etc. |\n","| **Imaging / lab results**| Doctor says “the X‑ray was normal”, “echo shows EF 55 %”, etc. |\n","| **Diagnoses / assessment**| Exact wording the physician uses (“I am concerned about a torn MCL”, “likely rotator‑cuff tendinopathy”). |\n","| **Orders & plan**        | Any prescription, imaging, referral, counseling, follow‑up time, lifestyle advice that the physician states. |\n","| **Patient agreement**   | Patient says “I understand”, “I’ll use a pill box”, etc. |\n","\n","--------------------------------------------------------------------\n","### What **must NOT** be inferred\n","\n","* Age or sex from name, voice, or pronouns alone.\n","* A diagnosis that the physician only speculates about.\n","* Dosage when only the drug name is mentioned.\n","* Follow‑up interval, medication frequency, or test result when not spoken.\n","\n","--------------------------------------------------------------------\n","### NOTE TEMPLATE (DO NOT MODIFY HEADINGS OR BULLET STYLE)\n","CHIEF COMPLAINT\n","...\n","\n","HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n","...\n","\n","MEDICAL HISTORY\n","...\n","\n","MEDICATIONS\n","...\n","\n","REVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n","...\n","\n","VITALS\n","...\n","\n","PHYSICAL EXAM\n","...\n","\n","ASSESSMENT\n","...\n","\n","PLAN\n","...\n","\n","PATIENT AGREEMENT / INSTRUCTIONS (optional)\n","...\n","\n","--------------------------------------------------------------------\n","When you have finished updating the note, output **exactly** the text of the\n","complete note (including all headings) and nothing else.\n","\"\"\""],"metadata":{"id":"J7GANLmEyu6H"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Load the model once (reuse across turns)\n","llm = Llama(\n","    model_path=model_path,\n","    n_ctx=8192,               # MedGemma / Gemma 3 supports up to 128k – adjust as needed\n","    n_threads=6,              # tune to your CPU\n","    n_gpu_layers=-1,          # offload to GPU if you have one\n","    verbose=False\n",")\n","\n","# ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# For each turn in your application:\n","# ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","\n","def generate_updated_note(previous_note: str, new_dialogue: str) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    previous_note: the full SOAP note from last turn (empty string on first turn)\n","    new_dialogue:   the latest chunk of conversation\n","    \"\"\"\n","    system_content = SYSTEM_PROMPT.strip()  # your long system instructions\n","\n","    # Combine system + current notes + new chunk into one strong user message\n","    # (Gemma-3/MedGemma does NOT have a native system role → put instructions in user)\n","    user_content = f\"\"\"CURRENT NOTES:\n","      {previous_note if previous_note.strip() else \"[No previous note yet]\"}\n","\n","      ---\n","\n","      DIALOGUE_CHUNK:\n","      {new_dialogue.strip()}\n","\n","      Please follow all the rules and template exactly as provided in the instructions above.\n","      Return ONLY the complete updated note – nothing else.\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    # Let llama.cpp handle special tokens via chat template\n","    response = llm.create_chat_completion(\n","        messages=[\n","            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system_content},   # many GGUF still accept it → gets prepended to first user\n","            {\"role\": \"user\",   \"content\": user_content},\n","        ],\n","        max_tokens=600,\n","        temperature=0.0,           # deterministic medical note → low/no temperature\n","        top_p=0.95,\n","        stop=[\"<end_of_turn>\", \"<|eot_id|>\"],\n","        # echo=False\n","    )\n","\n","    return response[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"].strip()\n","\n","\n","# Example usage in a loop\n","note_so_far = \"\"   # start empty\n","\n","# First turn\n","note_so_far = generate_updated_note(\n","    note_so_far,\n","    \"\"\"Patient: I've had chest pain for two days.\n","Doctor: Can you describe the pain? Is it sharp or dull?\"\"\"\n",")\n","\n","print(\"Updated note:\\n\", note_so_far)"],"metadata":{"id":"raSO6gii1Yno"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Next turn\n","note_so_far = generate_updated_note(\n","    note_so_far,\n","    \"\"\"Patient: It's sharp, worse when I breathe in.\n","Doctor: Any shortness of breath?\"\"\"\n",")\n","\n","print(\"Updated note:\\n\", note_so_far)"],"metadata":{"id":"iVZE2MWEDuC7"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}